--- A function that returns a literal list of ints on one path and a list of
--- values that can fail (int[text] items) on another is an internal error in
--- both modes, before the program runs.
---
--- Interpreted (crow run -i) and compiled (crow run), the same message:
---   p1.co: internal error: the lowered program disagrees with itself — a bug in
---   Crow, not in this program: fn pair_of: line 3: returns Tensor(Int, [2]) from
---   a body typed List(Result(Big))
---
--- Expected: [5, 4] then [3, 3] (or a refusal that names the two kinds, if a
--- list of ints and a list of values that can fail are meant to be two kinds).
--- With a = 2 ^ n in place of int[text] (no failure) it runs in both modes.
--- Found writing rosetta/honeycombs.co (a board size typed or the default).

fn pair_of[text]
    if text eq ''
        return [5, 4]
    a = int[text]
    return [a, a]

log[pair_of['']]
log[pair_of['3']]
